  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Fund Policy Advice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A series of commissioned pieces of policy research carried out by consultants via DAI Global UK under contract with the FCDO. Further information on such pieces are as follows. 1 - Channelling of Global Fund Development Assistance for Health (DAH) through country systems&#x2019; which looked at how aligning GFATM support with national systems improves the efficiency of Development Assistance for Health (DAH), an essential foundation for sustainability and longer-term economic development and welfare of ODA eligible countries. 2 - Integrating GHI programmes: Pooled Funding Models in Tanzania, Zimbabwe, and Ethiopia&#x2019; &#x2013; a piece of research to explore how GHIs can accelerate country-led progress towards achieving UHC and achieving the SDGs, assessing the potential benefits of pooled funding to harmonise and align development assistance, reduce transaction costs, and support development of systems which can ensure sustainability in the long term. 3 - A rapid review of support to development and capacity building on dashboards for Global Fund grant oversight at country level. Strengthening government systems to understand the role of dashboards in Global Fund governance and whether investments in dashboards support wider governance of the health system in 5 Global Fund priority countries.</narrative>
  </description>
